/Title (One of our projects is to design a two-stage rocket capable of reaching 100,000 feet, which would break the Canadian amateur rocketry record of 67,000 feet. We will also build our own launch rail, roughly 30 feet tall, first to get a more stable rail than those provided at competitions, and second to ensure an off-rail velocity high enough for the rocket to be stable. It will be made of steel from DMX antenna tower sections fitted with a guide rail, and an electric winch will be used to raise it to vertical.)
